cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mrwin: Causal Win Statistics for Hierarchical Composite Endpoints with Genetic Instruments"
version: "0.1.1.9000"
type: software
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata. The last tagged release is v0.1.1-arxiv-theory (2026-05-26), which accompanied the theory-only arXiv preprint; this entry describes the current development version."
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Thien Minh
    affiliation: "University of Medicine and Pharmacy at Ho Chi Minh City, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-1090-6228"
abstract: "mrwin is an R package for causal win statistics that integrates Mendelian randomization with hierarchical composite endpoints. It estimates the dose-standardised causal win ratio (DS-CWR) from adjacent polygenic-risk-score strata via instrument-standardised gradients and GLS pooling, with Fieller confidence intervals, multiplier-bootstrap or analytic influence-function variance including GWAS-weight uncertainty, ordinal inverse-probability weighting, and the Step-Down Pleiotropy Diagnostic. A compiled sub-quadratic win/loss kernel (up to three priority levels) makes the estimator feasible at biobank scale. Internal parity checks and a first external calibration grid (type-I error and coverage) have been completed; the full simulation study and an empirical application are in progress, so results should be treated as those of a development version."
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - win ratio
  - Mendelian randomization
  - instrumental variables
  - hierarchical composite endpoints
  - multiplier bootstrap
  - biostatistics
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nguyenminh2301/mrwin"
